{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"03acb970e607141fde6b7951d460002b0a2b042cf63f4311fcb9c52a84046d2c","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_0c29f8462a5599883d5f424053e089a37a4bf8be0d363140b8fb434deb2f1c4f","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a novel and interesting approach to sentence embeddings using self-attention. The writing is generally clear, but there are several areas for improvement in terminology consistency, mathematical notation, and figure labeling. Addressing these issues would enhance the clarity and reproducibility of the work.","paper_id":"BJC_jUqxe","paper_identity_sha256":"15b1d40569e6e1bcdba6a16575a23d36d57fd74507a8e3170f131209ed0325fe","prompt_identity_sha256":"912eb312ffef5ddaeb2d73fc1f6067265d7d20c9ee4a68fd02c1f04a1d2422e3","raw_response_sha256":"2b8b8cba125cd2671c6c9dcc385286b48c20702b8c7fb1cb4f2e3b910dc6bfa6","request_identity_sha256":"680c2aad04136cf14a2d31441eaf8cc273b3e1587cbd81d97d4632b1c002058f","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-016","SRC-017"],"review_text":"The paper is generally well-organized, with a clear progression from introduction to model description, related work, and experiments. However, there are several issues affecting clarity and precision. First, the introduction contains a grammatical error ('This including SkipThought vectors') and a typo ('netowkrs'), which detract from the professional quality of the writing. Second, the terminology is occasionally inconsistent; for example, the term 'annotation vector' is used interchangeably with 'attention vector' or 'summation weight vector' without a clear definition of which term is preferred, potentially confusing the reader. Third, the description of the model in Section 2.1 is somewhat dense, and the transition from the single-hop attention (Equation 5) to the multi-hop attention (Equation 6) could be smoother. The text states that 'we extend the w_s2 into a r-by-d_a matrix', but it would be clearer to explicitly state that this extension allows for multiple independent attention heads or hops. Finally, the experimental section (Section 4) could benefit from more detailed descriptions of the baselines, particularly regarding the specific hyperparameters used for the CNN and BiLSTM baselines, to ensure reproducibility.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is mostly consistent, but there are a few ambiguities. In Equation 5, the notation for the weight vector is \\mathbf{w}_{\\mathbf{s2}}, which is unusual; typically, boldface is used for vectors, but the subscript 's2' is also bolded, which is non-standard. It would be clearer to use \\mathbf{w}_{s2} or \\mathbf{v}. In Equation 6, the notation switches to \\mathbf{W}_{s2} for the matrix, which is consistent, but the transition from vector to matrix in the text could be more explicit. The definition of the penalization term P in Equation 8 is clear, but the explanation of why the Frobenius norm of (AA^T - I) is used as a proxy for KL divergence is somewhat hand-wavy. The text states that KL divergence is 'too computationally expensive', but it does not quantify this cost or explain why the dot product approximation is sufficient. Additionally, the notation for the hidden states H is defined as n-by-2u, but it is not explicitly stated whether the forward and backward hidden states are concatenated or summed, which could be a source of confusion for readers trying to reproduce the model.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The figures and tables are generally informative, but there are some issues with clarity. Figure 1 shows heatmaps of Yelp reviews, but the text in the heatmaps is small and may be difficult to read in print. The caption for Figure 1 is brief and does not explain how to interpret the heatmaps (e.g., what the color scale represents). Figure 2 compares models with and without the penalization term, but the caption does not clearly state which column corresponds to which model, although the text does. It would be clearer to label the columns directly in the figure. Figure 3 is similar to Figure 2 but for the Yelp dataset, and it suffers from the same issues. Table 1, 2, and 3 are clear and well-formatted, but Table 2 could benefit from a note explaining the source of the baseline results (e.g., whether they are from the original papers or re-implemented). The overall presentation of the figures is adequate, but improvements in labeling and caption detail would enhance readability.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"decb075e43f7edc3a2b90abe1a315d6630263d776daad72ce075b753e59d4f13","paper_id":"BJC_jUqxe","paper_ordinal":26,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"2b8b8cba125cd2671c6c9dcc385286b48c20702b8c7fb1cb4f2e3b910dc6bfa6","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJC_jUqxe","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"3a7a34f742a1d87b3e990730a36f2d856b8a80605beb3803393790252f2c96be","request_identity_sha256":"680c2aad04136cf14a2d31441eaf8cc273b3e1587cbd81d97d4632b1c002058f","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":1090,"prompt_tokens":16633,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17723},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"680c2aad04136cf14a2d31441eaf8cc273b3e1587cbd81d97d4632b1c002058f","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}